  "rendered": {
    "title": "Sharper tool errors, safer hosted auth, and a quieter Windows Git",
    "intro": "Today's nightly focuses on trust and clarity: chat surfaces tool failures in a way people can actually act on, mobile makes it obvious when a remote agent is required, and the server side closes a cross-user auth race on Aura Web while calming Windows Desktop's flashing Git consoles. Under the hood, dev-loop sessions now require a stable identity so telemetry and rate limits stay coherent across restarts.",
    "entries": [
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-1",
        "time_label": "12:35 AM",
        "started_at": "2026-08-31T07:35:01.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-08-31T07:35:01.000Z",
        "title": "Dev-loop runs get a mandatory, stable session identity",
        "summary": "Automaton start parameters now require a session ID up front so dev-loop restarts stay coherent with rate limiting and telemetry.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "`aura_session_id` is now a required string on `AutomatonStartParams` rather than an optional field, so dev-loop bootstrap and continuation requests can't reach the harness without one and Cloudflare's per-session rate bucket stops resetting on every restart.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "c649557c235b97ce6f94ced0a943e042b20fe225"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Server- and harness-side identity validation, start-params assembly, and tests were updated together so the stable dev-loop session ID flows end-to-end into the outbound `X-Aura-Session-Id` header.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "c649557c235b97ce6f94ced0a943e042b20fe225"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-2",
        "time_label": "7:26 AM",
        "started_at": "2026-08-31T14:26:24.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-08-31T14:26:24.000Z",
        "title": "Hosted workspace files stop crossing user auth boundaries",
        "summary": "A concurrency bug on Aura Web that could resolve a hosted file request under another user's token has been fixed by scoping agent lookups to the incoming JWT.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Hosted workspace file handlers no longer route through `AgentInstanceService::get_instance`, which shared a process-wide cached session and could re-issue a correctly authorized request under a different user's token, producing false 404s on Aura Web under concurrent load.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "10890eb06aafb912f34794ce5e334cd2e07535c7"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "The handler now resolves the parent agent using the request's own JWT via the network client (or the local agent service as a fallback) and a new auth-race integration test locks in the behavior.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "10890eb06aafb912f34794ce5e334cd2e07535c7"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-3",
        "time_label": "8:21 AM",
        "started_at": "2026-08-31T15:21:32.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-08-31T15:22:11.000Z",
        "title": "Clearer tool errors in chat and a more honest mobile composer",
        "summary": "Chat now renders structured tool error responses, and the mobile input bar makes it obvious when a remote agent is required before you can send.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Generic tool blocks now parse error results into a dedicated response card with a title, message, HTTP status/code metadata, guidance bullets, and a formatted \"Try again in…\" hint when the tool returns a retry delay.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "b4fcc9610712db42c6269b96816bdfae7ecb0716"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "The mobile chat input bar gains a disabled-state notice and a \"remote required\" status pill so users understand why send is unavailable, backed by a new test suite covering tap-to-send behavior.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "f010d68bbd402146c29c6d173c4c210a41462047"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-4",
